WEBVTT

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.670
Why?! Why!?

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:01.280
Just as planned. My old school is pretty strong.

00:01:01.280 --> 00:01:03.120
As long as they're in order...

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.380
My data didn't forsee such a situation.

00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:09.250
I can't believe Oarai is getting cornered...

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:12.090
Being careless is pretty scary, isn't it?

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:16.560
One of the many obstacles in our quest to achieve our ideals...

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.850
...lies within ourselves.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:22.760
I'm sorry! It's my fault! I was completely fooled!

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.270
This isn't your fault at all, Yukari-san!

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:28.270
But if this goes on, we might lose the first match!

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:30.360
That absolutely cannot happen!

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.190
If that happens, then that would be the end of the road.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:54.010
To the faraway skies, we aim our finite youth and SHOOT!

00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:00.220
Our times together is the most valuable thing

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:05.290
How many words have we exchanged?

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:10.940
Glide and ride, the magic that connects all our thoughts

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:16.900
No matter what obstacle we faced, we've overcome them all

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:21.910
The road ahead remains unknown, but I want to jump in

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:27.210
And push open a new door

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:31.710
I want open it together with you

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:37.170
Even now it's true, and always will be

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:43.180
The future we hold in our hands is the symphony we create together

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:47.890
Let's lift up each others' dreams and mix them all together

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:55.860
With our hands clasped together and with these tears we've shed

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:01.520
Let's build a rainbow in the sky

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.000
Where is it?

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:39.250
Where is it hidden?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.350
Grid G5, unknown detected on level four.

00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:44.660
Tagging object as Tango One.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:47.830
Judging from its size, the unknown is possibly a tank.

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:49.000
Yes, we did it!

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.470
Now you've done it!

00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:51.860
Isn't that pretty bad?!

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:53.430
That's really bad!

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.340
My condolences...

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.400
Please don't lose heart!

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.310
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:09.670
Extra! Extra! Extra!

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:15.480
How do you feel about Kawashima-san repeating a year?

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.050
Is there any hope for her?

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:18.190
I don't know...

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.560
What will happen to Kawashima-san?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.150
Will she graduate with us, piyon?

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:23.240
Everyone, please calm down!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:26.790
It's times like this that we shouldn't focus on the worst,

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:28.480
but think more positively!

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:30.120
Don't worry!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.280
We'll let you know once we get the true story!

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.800
Okay...

00:04:36.310 --> 00:04:38.650
What the heck is this article?!

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:39.630
Nice chair, right?

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.130
Oh, yes... sorry. Please.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.500
You can stay seated.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.090
You're the student council president now, Isuzu-chan.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:46.960
Thank you.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.350
I will do my best to not bring shame to you, Chairman Kadotani.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.390
Please support her as the vice student council president, Akiyama-san.

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:54.240
Yes! Understood!

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.380
Kawashima-senpai, now that you're here for another year,

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:59.610
there's no need to rush the PR handover.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.980
I'm not repeating a year!

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:02.740
Ah, then that article...

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.760
I just couldn't get into a university!

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:07.560
It seems that the rumors became about her "repeating a year".

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.690
Check this out.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:13.100
"You can take the test as a remembrance"?

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:18.750
Ankou University, Konjac Fisheries College, and Natto International University have the same recommendation, huh?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.890
Anzu and I can probably get into the same National College,

00:05:22.890 --> 00:05:25.400
but Momo-chan seems to be having a hard time applying anywhere...

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:27.220
You won't be a repeater, but a ronin.

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.970
Everyone's just making a scandal out of it!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:34.470
It's fine! Even Moltke and Patton weren't excellent at studies!

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:37.120
Shut it! It's not like I've failed!

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.740
Then how about you focus on studying instead of looking for tanks?

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.600
Tanks?

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.690
Momo-chan's been working hard on looking for a tank before graduating...

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:45.620
Tanks?

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.310
Are there more tanks here?

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:49.450
We just found another one.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:53.910
After 20 years, they're finally holding the Winter Continuous Track Cup!

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.840
It was held to commemorate the founding of the Senshado League,

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:00.230
but it's been on hiatus all this time!

00:06:00.230 --> 00:06:04.820
After the start of the Pro Leagues and with eyes on the World Tournament, they decided to hold this again!

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:09.120
I wanted to find a new tank before the Cup starts.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.800
It's all I can do for you girls before I leave.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.220
So that the school may not abolished again,

00:06:16.220 --> 00:06:19.370
I want to turn Oarai's Senshado into a cornerstone!

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:23.490
I see...

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:27.190
She did it in secret for us...

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:30.140
It's like Sanada's army besieging the Toishi Castle...

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:31.870
Like the Battle of Pharsalus!

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:33.410
Like the Bloodless Surrender of Edo.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:35.160
No, it's like the Gran Sasso Raid!

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.080
That's it!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.840
But vanishing as a one-man party is pitiful, nyaa...

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:44.480
For the past three years, Kawashima-san had perfect attendance with no tardiness and absences!

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:47.840
I want to celebrate her graduation and her new school, piyo!

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:49.620
I wanted to race to the chequered flag together.

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:51.570
Can't we do something for her?

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:57.980
It seems that Prez and Vice Prez's Shimofusadai National University has an AO entrance exam.

00:06:57.980 --> 00:06:59.650
AO entrance exam?

00:06:59.650 --> 00:07:01.940
It means you can get admitted if you have a special talent.

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:02.610
Ay!

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:03.270
Oh!

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.240
That's why it's called AO!

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.030
I see!

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.580
That's not it!

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.130
Then can she get through with Senshado?

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.800
She probably could!

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:17.320
Onee-chan got a tank scholarship and decided to study abroad in Niedersächsische Universität.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.950
She's in Germany right now!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:24.750
I believe Megumi, Azumi and Rumi from enrolled via sports scholarships during university selection!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.170
Let's go with that, then.

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:29.970
We'll make Kawashima the Commander in the Winter Cup and be the victors!

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.010
Good idea!

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:33.300
We'll work hard for senpai!

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.100
A! A! O!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.760
Yes! We'll stop it at Match Point!

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.640
We'll K.O. our way through the matches!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.980
With no losses!

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.690
Kawashima-senpai as the Commander...

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.720
Although it makes me a bit uneasy...

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.650
We'll be fine as long as we heed Commander Nishizumi's advice.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:50.100
A puppet commander, huh...

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.110
Yes.

00:07:50.110 --> 00:07:54.450
Nishizumi-san, as Vice Commander do your best and let senpai take all the glory!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:55.510
Ah, alright!

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.600
Then, everyone!

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.730
To prevent Kawashima-senpai's repeating...

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.590
Oh, no, um...

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:06.250
To make sure that senpai gets into university,

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:07.040
let's give our best!

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:08.440
Yeah!

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:09.050
No...

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:09.710
Repeating!

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:10.590
No...

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.220
Repeating!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.060
No...

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.470
Repeating!

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:17.490
Shut up! I'm not repeating! Stop it!

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.060
Momo-chan as the Commander?

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:19.610
Yes!

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:20.950
I'm really sorry...

00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:23.020
Sorry you had to do all this for her.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.600
Then, before the Winter Cup, we gotta find a tank!

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:28.650
We'll go look for it instead!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:31.480
Kawashima-senpai, please focus on studying for your exams.

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:34.810
So, any ideas about where the tank might be?

00:08:34.810 --> 00:08:38.290
We detected something below decks, but will you do it?

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:39.280
It's pretty dangerous.

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:41.690
Looks like Sodoko will guide us there.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:46.160
Hello!

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:46.710
Hello!

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.600
Hello!

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.770
Hello!

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.130
Hello!

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:51.670
This isn't dangerous at all!

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.260
You have no idea.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:56.740
We're still in the upper half of the ship.

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.920
The students here are quiet and stick to the rules,

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:04.960
but the lower we go, the public order gets worse.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:09.330
And beyond that point is the "Johannesburg of Oarai"!

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:14.600
Even the Student Council has no power here: a real lawless territory.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.200
We event took these down recently!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:20.620
Shall I cut through them?

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:33.370
Is it really okay to keep going?

00:09:33.370 --> 00:09:36.490
Don't worry, I'll rein them in.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.800
They're staring intensely at us...

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.240
Don't look them in the eyes...

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.910
Hold it right there!

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.950
You tryin' to enter without permission?

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.980
Whose permission do I need to move within the school grounds?!

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:03.580
I'm free to pass as I please!

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.040
What's up with this one?

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.540
I am the former Morals Committee President and
current Committee Adviser, Sono Midoriko!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:12.170
Your skirts are way too long!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.590
And what's with all the trash here? Clean it up!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.880
Why don't you do it yourself, then?

00:10:18.090 --> 00:10:20.760
Why would I do that? Clean up after your own mess!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:22.300
Shut up, Kappa!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.620
Looks like we have to teach you a lesson, Kappa!

00:10:25.410 --> 00:10:27.430
What are you doing!?

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.750
Look at you. Let's go...

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:59.610
Sorry, Mako-san! I couldn't stop!

00:11:09.490 --> 00:11:10.920
Is this a dead end?

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.540
How did they just disappear?

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:19.670
Over here, eh?

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.680
Yukari-san! Are you okay?

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:46.130
It's dawn! Ho!

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:53.650
Let's sail further than the Seven Seas!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:59.280
Hey! Ride the breeze, don't stop!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:04.910
There's nothing scary about the Sargasso Sea!

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:07.760
Row, row, row!

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.620
Feast, Feast, Feast!

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:13.410
Drink, drink, drink!

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:16.230
Throw up, throw up, throw up!

00:12:16.230 --> 00:12:21.510
Plunder and split the booty

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:21.510
You need to order something first before you sit.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:25.220
Oh, right... Do you have a menu?

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.140
Why'd we have that here?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:27.970
Sorry!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:28.930
What should we order?

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:29.700
Well...

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:31.460
I'll have a milk tea.

00:12:31.460 --> 00:12:32.390
Same for me, then!

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:33.460
Milk Cocoa!

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:34.610
I want a café au lait!

00:12:34.610 --> 00:12:36.000
Milkshake!

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:39.970
What do have we here? Babies?

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:44.240
You ladies should go back to land and drink some from your mama.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:46.280
We'll leave after our business is done.

00:12:45.750 --> 00:12:51.160
Handsomely lift the glass of rum

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.160
Where's Sodoko?

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:54.450
Hey... Sodoko...?

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:57.040
The former Morals Committee President with the Kappa hairstyle.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:58.380
Kappa?

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:01.840
By Kappa do you mean the board that got thrown in here?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:02.580
Yes, that board.

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:05.400
Kappa is cleaning up over there.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:11.240
Hey! Get over here and give me a hand!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:12.730
Release Sodoko.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:14.600
Once she's done cleaning.

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:16.560
Do the rest yourself.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:19.180
Let's go back.

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:21.250
Get this thing off me, first!

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:26.030
Hold it! You think you can take her and just walk outta here?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:30.850
Why are you on our turf anyway?

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:33.000
Well... We're looking for a tank...

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.910
Tank? Who are you people?

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:40.750
When askin' questions, isn't it polite to name yourselves first?

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.010
I'm the Student Council President, Izusu Hana.

00:13:43.010 --> 00:13:45.090
Vice President, Akiyama Yukari.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.740
PR Manager, Takebe Saori.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.570
Um... I'm the Commander...

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.640
Commander?

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:50.680
Y-Yes... for the tanks...

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:52.170
Tanks?

00:13:52.170 --> 00:13:55.770
Oh, you mean landships? The ones which look like soft-shelled turtles.

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.550
Yeah... I'm the Commander of those, Nishizumi Miho.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.860
Driver for the soft-shelled turtle, Reizei Mako.

00:14:00.860 --> 00:14:03.590
There are signs of a tank around here.

00:14:03.590 --> 00:14:05.220
Can you tell us anything about it?

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.490
You think I'd just tell you?

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.200
If you win against us in a duel, I would.

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.070
Duel?

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.400
If we win, you release Sodoko, too.

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:14.960
Okay!

00:14:14.960 --> 00:14:17.860
Then I'm up first!

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.210
Untie this knot!

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.400
Oh, it's an Anchor Bend!

00:14:24.370 --> 00:14:25.590
What?

00:14:25.760 --> 00:14:29.160
I'm up next! Can you decipher this?

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.480
You should respect your elders at home!

00:14:34.480 --> 00:14:35.660
That's correct!

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.090
That's our radio operator!

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:39.910
We'll have this for the next match!

00:14:39.910 --> 00:14:42.100
Ready?

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:42.910
Go!

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.240
Incredible! She pressed down on the joint!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.320
Mako-san is awesome!

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:59.580
She must've trained her fingers while driving the tank!

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.580
What a hassle! Let's settle this with a brawl!

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:03.850
Erm, uhm...

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.220
Wait, this is dangerous!

00:15:06.220 --> 00:15:07.270
Uhm!

00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:21.060
I'm really sorry! Can we please talk it out?!

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:24.770
Nishizumi-dono, good job!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.850
Miho-san is used to evading shells, after all.

00:15:28.380 --> 00:15:29.570
Pretty good...

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.960
Now that it's come to this...

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:32.240
All of us should...

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.880
That's enough!

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.060
Cap'n...

00:15:50.710 --> 00:15:52.780
Ye fellas...

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.550
...are almost as good as Captain Kidd.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:59.430
Though me and Captain Kidd...

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:00.680
...have never met.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:08.320
Here be the famous drink from <i>Donzoko</i>,
the non-alcoholic rum, Habanero Club!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.110
Looks delicious.

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:11.640
I wouldn't do that if I were you.

00:16:16.800 --> 00:16:17.990
Spicy!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.350
Told ya.

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:23.710
Even Captain Drake be runnin' away from this hellish pepper rum.

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:25.370
It be a drinking contest!

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.060
I'll do it.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:17:01.640
You've got quite the stomach, but this is far from over!

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:03.210
Let's keep going, then!

00:17:16.730 --> 00:17:17.760
Feel better yet?

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:18.740
No.

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.540
Hana?

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:32.040
Not yet...

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.400
Another one, please!

00:17:33.590 --> 00:17:38.620
Ye pretend to be fine... But ye stomach must be burning red.

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:40.870
Tomorrow's gonna be rough, y'know?

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:04.170
I'd like another one, please.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.410
Hana, are you all right?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.410
Cap'n!

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:18.130
I feel warm all over!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:21.130
Ye ain't the usual folk...

00:18:21.130 --> 00:18:25.320
As promised, we'll return her. No strings attached.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:29.000
"Return"? I'm not some kind of school equipment!

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:30.040
Excuse me...

00:18:30.040 --> 00:18:31.170
What is it?

00:18:31.170 --> 00:18:33.840
Can you tell us where the tank is?

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.590
Tanks? They're no ships...

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.840
Don't ye drive them around on land?

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.720
I'm not interested in that kind of stuff!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.100
Please, we need a new tank!

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:46.680
It's for Kawashima-senpai, too!

00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:52.060
Who's that? I ain't obligated to help some rat I don't know.

00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:55.070
Though I don't know what a rat worth helping looks like, anyway.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:57.610
Cap'n! Maybe they're talkin' about Momo-san?

00:18:57.610 --> 00:19:00.160
Momo-san?

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.030
Did something happen to her?!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.910
Look at this!

00:19:03.910 --> 00:19:04.870
I can't believe it...

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.540
Momo-san is in danger! We gotta help her!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:10.750
We wouldn't be lazing around here if it weren't for her!

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:12.460
You mean Kawashima-senpai?

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:18.010
We were about to be expelled back then, but she covered for us!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:21.280
We're trying to get her into a university via Senshado!

00:19:21.280 --> 00:19:23.580
For this we need a new tank!

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:25.510
What does this "tank" thing look like?

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.720
Like this:

00:19:26.720 --> 00:19:33.190
A car with thick armor, and maybe a long cannon!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.670
Could it be?!

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:42.410
Wow, incredible!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:46.480
I always use this as a smoking machine. Who would've thought it was a tank?

00:19:46.480 --> 00:19:47.370
Delicious!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:51.000
Isn't it? Smoked to perfection with sakura chips!

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.380
How do we use this fella?

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.710
To start, should we have the Automobile Club restore it?

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.840
But who will operate this tank?

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:02.220
Seems the transmission and brakes were already modified, so...

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:03.930
Two drivers...

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:07.810
We probably won't need the MG, but two main gunners...

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.990
Plus the commander, that's five crew!

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:13.160
I'll ride it!

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.440
It's a landship, ain't it?

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:19.780
If it's a ship, then it's our turn!

00:20:19.780 --> 00:20:22.110
I'm "Tornado" Ogin!

00:20:22.110 --> 00:20:23.570
"Great Waves" Flint!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:25.490
"Explosive Cyclone" Rum!

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.740
"Sargasso" Murakami!

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:30.910
That's four, we just need one more...

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.870
"Fresh Whitebait Rice Bowl" Cutlass.

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.430
So she was a student, too...

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:40.880
A ninth vehicle! I didn't expect that we'd get to fix a new tank.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.720
But why does it smell so delicious?

00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:47.090
Maybe they left some meat scented armoatic?

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:49.610
Oh, delicious!

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:51.180
The smoked salmon's pretty good, too!

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.600
So you're the ones who'll be joining?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.640
Of course!

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:56.480
We want to return Momo-san's favor!

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.270
We'll do our best!

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:02.190
I swear on the Seven Seas, ye not gonna repeat!

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.960
I told you, I'm not repeating a year!

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:10.520
Oarai's first repeater... how unfortunate.

00:21:10.520 --> 00:21:14.750
It's good that Darjeeling-sama has already decided to go to the UK...

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:18.980
I can finally taste authentic afternoon tea.

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:24.140
But in some ways, this tournament is more important than the one last summer.

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:27.390
I hope I can taste victory before departing.

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:31.850
The future does not start tomorrow, but today.

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:33.560
Oh, ah, yes!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.610
The Kuromorimine captain has gone to Germany.

00:21:38.610 --> 00:21:40.000
Yes.

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.650
What will Katyusha-sama do next?

00:21:42.650 --> 00:21:46.300
It seems that she will go to a Russian school.

00:21:46.300 --> 00:21:49.300
Then she should start learning Russian now.

00:21:49.300 --> 00:21:53.330
I tried teaching her, but she fell asleep quickly!

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:55.580
What are you two talking about?

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:58.030
And you, how long are you gonna stick around?

00:21:58.030 --> 00:22:01.710
It's comfortable here, so I'll stay for a bit longer.

00:22:01.710 --> 00:22:04.110
I told you to speak Japanese!

00:22:04.110 --> 00:22:05.720
Just a little longer.

00:22:05.150 --> 00:22:05.720
Oh, I see!

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:09.450
Anyway, I'm sure we're gonna win this time!

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:11.640
We're good at fighting in winter!

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:13.890
We must win no matter what!

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.310
Understood!

00:22:16.950 --> 00:22:21.560
It seems that it's gonna be a showdown among Pravda, St. Gloriana, Oarai...

00:22:21.560 --> 00:22:25.110
...and us, Saunders.

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:29.700
Even without Nishizumi Maho, we shouldn't understimate Kuromorimine.

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:32.660
Yes. It all depends on the bracket draw.

00:22:32.660 --> 00:22:34.290
Let's hope we get lucky!

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:38.260
If we win, maybe he'll notice me...

00:22:38.260 --> 00:22:41.580
Is it really okay for me to be the new Commander?

00:22:41.580 --> 00:22:45.730
Don't fret over the results. You should find your own Senshado.

00:22:46.690 --> 00:22:47.800
Yes!

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.930
Everyone, the heavens side with us!

00:22:51.180 --> 00:22:52.300
Yeah!

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:53.970
Remember, we will let everyone know...

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:57.850
...that Anzio is not weak. No! We're strong!

00:22:57.850 --> 00:23:05.720
Duce! Duce! Duce!

00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:08.900
What did we lack during last summer's matches?

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:10.160
Our mental strength!

00:23:10.160 --> 00:23:11.660
I agree!

00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:13.660
So what should we do in the upcoming matches?

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:15.910
With great resolve, charge at the enemy!

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:17.870
A worthy man always charges!

00:23:18.120 --> 00:23:19.780
The bird who charges get the early worm!

00:23:19.780 --> 00:23:21.670
Follow the most important of the 36 stratagems and charge!

00:23:21.670 --> 00:23:23.420
We have nothing to lose if we charge!

00:23:23.590 --> 00:23:25.020
Less talking, more charging!

00:23:24.540 --> 00:23:28.510
Continuous Track Cup
Strategy Meeting

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:28.510
One charge after another!

00:23:34.030 --> 00:23:36.470
Let's join the Winter Cup!

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.690
Winter is a time when everything must slumber.

00:23:39.690 --> 00:23:41.520
It's not the time for fighting.

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.910
I'd like to see everyone again...

00:23:44.370 --> 00:23:47.380
It is true that we must treasure the company of others,

00:23:47.380 --> 00:23:50.350
but solitude is just as important.

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:55.910
41st Continuous Track Cup Draw Lots

00:24:00.390 --> 00:24:02.970
Oarai Girls School, number four.

00:24:08.980 --> 00:24:11.470
The first match is against BC Freedom Academy.

00:24:11.470 --> 00:24:13.270
What kind of school are they?

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:14.680
You put us up against the victors from last summer!

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:16.470
You're the one who drew the ballot!

00:24:16.470 --> 00:24:18.120
You puttin' the blame on me?!

00:24:18.120 --> 00:24:20.560
I'm not blaming you. It's <i>your</i> fault.

00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:23.600
Transfer students like you love to lie.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.400
You escalator students do nothing but look down on others!

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:27.980
What did you say, you outsider?!

00:24:27.980 --> 00:24:32.670
Can we not fight over trivial things? The cake will go bad.

00:24:32.670 --> 00:24:36.200
BC Freedom Academy seems to clash all the time.

00:24:36.200 --> 00:24:36.940
Yeah...

00:24:36.940 --> 00:24:44.000
They 're an aristocratic school, but the original students and the high school transfers seem to be hostile towards each other.

00:24:44.000 --> 00:24:47.750
They're always eliminated in the first match, so there's not much data on them...

00:24:47.750 --> 00:24:49.900
Please leave that to me!

00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:15.780
Erm, I'm currently inside BC Freedom Academy!

00:25:19.620 --> 00:25:28.130
No to forks! No to spoons!
Equal meals!
Enforce the taste of the commoners
Soy sauce on the dining table!
Curry udon as well!

00:25:20.760 --> 00:25:22.260
Meals!

00:25:22.260 --> 00:25:25.820
No more escargot meals!
No more foie gras meals!

00:25:26.340 --> 00:25:28.530
Serve udon in the school cafeteria!

00:25:28.530 --> 00:25:30.930
If we serve that, our dignity will suffer.

00:25:30.930 --> 00:25:34.810
They say those girls couldn't even use a knife and fork properly.

00:25:34.810 --> 00:25:40.050
It looks like there is a deep division between the students.

00:25:40.050 --> 00:25:44.370
Eh, from here on out I'll be heading to the tank storehouse. Let's go and take a look!

00:25:46.040 --> 00:25:47.530
We'll be the flag tank.

00:25:47.530 --> 00:25:48.120
Yeah!

00:25:48.120 --> 00:25:50.090
Oh, no. Leave that to us.

00:25:50.090 --> 00:25:50.930
Indeed! Indeed!

00:25:50.930 --> 00:25:53.370
Just decide on the flag tank with rock-paper-scissors!

00:25:53.370 --> 00:25:56.150
We can't settle this with such a half-assed method!

00:25:55.210 --> 00:25:57.060
You dare defy Marie-sama?

00:25:57.060 --> 00:25:58.890
You're getting cocky, you outsider!

00:25:58.890 --> 00:26:01.700
Same to you! What do you sheltered escalator students know?

00:26:01.700 --> 00:26:04.830
You should just keep close to our asses!

00:26:04.910 --> 00:26:07.790
If you're the one's going up front, I'll just shoot your ass!

00:26:07.790 --> 00:26:11.320
Just look at how barbaric these girls are! Just leave the match to us!

00:26:11.320 --> 00:26:14.590
Someone who hasn't gone through an examination war can't fight!

00:26:14.590 --> 00:26:17.380
What did you say? Just watch us destroy the enemy's flag tank!

00:26:17.380 --> 00:26:19.930
Watch me destroy yours first!

00:26:19.930 --> 00:26:22.200
I'll beat you at your own game!

00:26:22.200 --> 00:26:23.410
Ouch!

00:26:23.410 --> 00:26:28.000
The team's split apart! I don't think they can even fight in Senshado!

00:26:28.000 --> 00:26:30.690
That is all! Akiyama Yukari, signing out!

00:26:39.390 --> 00:26:41.170
The cake looks delicious...

00:26:41.170 --> 00:26:43.760
Mako-san, that's not what you should be looking at...

00:26:43.760 --> 00:26:47.100
But will they be able to participate in the match like that?

00:26:47.100 --> 00:26:49.140
They look like they'll just shoot each other.

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:52.440
It's possible that we might win the first match without doing anything...

00:26:52.440 --> 00:26:54.170
Well, that helps!

00:26:54.170 --> 00:26:57.840
Forget about the enemy! Are our preparations going well?!

00:26:57.840 --> 00:26:59.850
How about our spplies of AP rounds and antifreeze?!

00:26:59.850 --> 00:27:01.690
What's the tactics and operation name?!

00:27:00.880 --> 00:27:03.460
Uhm, we'll think about that.

00:27:03.460 --> 00:27:07.410
Even for a bit, please study for your exams during this time, Commander!

00:27:07.880 --> 00:27:08.850
Commander...

00:27:08.850 --> 00:27:11.840
Please leave the preparations to us, Commander!

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:12.860
Commander?!

00:27:12.860 --> 00:27:14.920
Calm down, Momo-chan.

00:27:14.920 --> 00:27:17.590
Will we be okay?

00:28:25.330 --> 00:28:27.850
It looks like the enemy team hasn't arrived...

00:28:27.850 --> 00:28:28.980
Did they oversleep?!

00:28:28.980 --> 00:28:31.970
If they don't arrive, we win by default, right?

00:28:31.970 --> 00:28:32.430
Probably...

00:28:32.430 --> 00:28:34.270
We're lucky, then!

00:28:34.270 --> 00:28:36.770
Our ninth vehicle hasn't arrived yet!

00:28:36.770 --> 00:28:39.140
They never made it to practice, either.

00:28:39.140 --> 00:28:40.610
What kind of tank do they have?

00:28:40.610 --> 00:28:42.610
What kind of people are riding it?

00:28:42.610 --> 00:28:45.700
They said they'll be arriving here by boat instead of train, didn't they?

00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:46.270
Yeah...

00:28:46.270 --> 00:28:49.000
They said they were at the harbor when they called me...

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:51.280
Oh, the Shark Team's here!

00:28:56.570 --> 00:28:58.590
That's the Shark team?! A shark?!

00:28:58.590 --> 00:28:59.560
Are those pirates?!

00:28:59.560 --> 00:29:00.480
Warriors?!

00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:02.000
Gallant samurai...

00:29:40.150 --> 00:29:41.450
A pillbug?

00:29:41.450 --> 00:29:42.600
Oh, it does look like one.

00:29:42.600 --> 00:29:44.180
It looks like a baked sweet potato!

00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:46.560
That tank is called a "Mark IV".

00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:49.120
From its shape, it was called the "diamond tank",

00:29:49.120 --> 00:29:53.780
And it was one of the first to fight in tank-on-tank battles!

00:29:53.780 --> 00:29:56.510
This is the Shark Team, our new crew!

00:29:57.200 --> 00:29:58.270
Kept you waiting, huh?

00:29:58.270 --> 00:29:59.890
She looks like trouble.

00:29:59.890 --> 00:30:00.690
Looks like a pirate.

00:30:00.690 --> 00:30:01.860
A thief, a thief...

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:03.480
The hell did you kids just say?!

00:30:03.480 --> 00:30:06.880
I'm turning you into shark food.

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:08.840
You don't need to worry about them.

00:30:08.840 --> 00:30:12.410
They may have the mouth of a sailor, but they care for their mates.

00:30:12.410 --> 00:30:14.290
Everyone is already here, right?

00:30:14.290 --> 00:30:16.830
Yes. Do you need anything, Commander?

00:30:24.170 --> 00:30:30.050
To all who have come all this way just to help me, including the new ones from the ship...

00:30:30.050 --> 00:30:32.440
I am deeply thankful!

00:30:34.690 --> 00:30:37.310
Let's all unite and do our best!

00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:39.060
Yeah!

00:30:39.060 --> 00:30:43.420
We'll do our best, Commander Momo-san!
Even if it's our first time doing Senshado!

00:30:43.420 --> 00:30:46.510
Still, it looks like the enemy team has yet to arrive.

00:30:46.510 --> 00:30:48.160
Will they be participating?

00:30:48.160 --> 00:30:50.360
We still have five minutes before the match...

00:30:50.360 --> 00:30:52.320
Will we really win by default?

00:30:52.320 --> 00:30:53.090
They're here!

00:30:59.870 --> 00:31:05.920
Now, then. We will now begin the match between Oarai Girls and BC Freedom Academy.

00:31:05.920 --> 00:31:06.500
Bow!

00:31:06.500 --> 00:31:07.890
Let's have a good game!

00:31:07.890 --> 00:31:09.630
Let's have a good game!

00:31:10.190 --> 00:31:12.500
Hey! Have the Commander bow her head!

00:31:12.500 --> 00:31:14.050
Why don't you do it yourself?!

00:31:14.050 --> 00:31:17.370
Why do I need to bow my head?

00:31:17.370 --> 00:31:18.770
You're both escalator students!

00:31:18.770 --> 00:31:21.260
You're the one in charge of the dirty work!

00:32:31.770 --> 00:32:35.960
We're the flag tank this time, huh?
Our responsibility's pretty huge...

00:32:35.960 --> 00:32:39.720
Nishizumi probably wanted Kawashima to take all the glory.

00:32:39.890 --> 00:32:43.950
Our opponent BC Freedom Academy has pretty high mobility.

00:32:43.950 --> 00:32:47.770
This match is a Flag Battle, so we'll keep our flag tank safe.

00:32:47.770 --> 00:32:51.820
Don't play too defensively, and focus on the enemy flag tank.

00:32:51.820 --> 00:32:57.090
According to my intel, it seems that the enemy is split apart and has poor coordination.

00:32:57.090 --> 00:33:00.310
Which means the flag tank won't have enough defenders.

00:33:00.310 --> 00:33:01.160
Let's attack!

00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:04.480
Uhm, I think we should properly scout first...

00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:06.630
You're pretty cautious... Oh well...

00:33:06.630 --> 00:33:09.060
Let's send Duck and Leopon out to scout.

00:33:09.060 --> 00:33:10.970
Yes, I think that's the best course of action.

00:33:10.970 --> 00:33:12.840
Copy that!

00:33:13.080 --> 00:33:16.750
We copy as well! Heading to the recon perimeter now!

00:33:43.940 --> 00:33:47.920
Duck here! Encountered four Somuas heading south at high speed!

00:33:47.920 --> 00:33:54.430
Uhm, Leopon here. Four ARL 44s aggressively heading towards the south.

00:33:54.430 --> 00:33:57.830
Which means the remaining two are probably here.

00:33:57.830 --> 00:33:59.840
Just what are they up to?

00:33:59.840 --> 00:34:02.420
Maybe the Escalator and Examination groups are fighting for glory

00:34:02.420 --> 00:34:05.670
and they both want to get to our flag tank first?

00:34:05.670 --> 00:34:07.060
Such "Freedom", eh?

00:34:07.060 --> 00:34:10.180
That means their flag tank is undefended, right?

00:34:10.180 --> 00:34:14.290
Yes. They have ten tanks, so there's one escort tank with the flag.

00:34:14.290 --> 00:34:17.010
The ideal place for the flag tank would be a hill, huh?

00:34:17.010 --> 00:34:18.800
There's a river behind it.

00:34:18.800 --> 00:34:20.080
Looks like there's a bridge.

00:34:20.080 --> 00:34:20.930
All right!

00:34:20.930 --> 00:34:24.280
We'll go through the shallows, go behind the enemy, and attack from the bridge!

00:34:24.280 --> 00:34:26.010
I think that's a great plan!

00:34:26.010 --> 00:34:30.260
Duck and Leopon, please follow the Somuas and ARLs.

00:34:30.260 --> 00:34:33.260
Understood! I'm marking the opponent from the end line.

00:34:33.260 --> 00:34:35.370
Alert us as soon as something changes.

00:34:35.370 --> 00:34:37.780
Okay! We're holding our position.

00:34:39.500 --> 00:34:44.040
Erm, okay. The main force will move in a column and go through the forest at ten 'o clock.

00:34:44.040 --> 00:34:46.280
Make sure you watch your surroundings.

00:34:46.280 --> 00:34:49.680
Which means... Erm... What was it?

00:34:49.680 --> 00:34:51.060
Your orders, please.

00:34:51.230 --> 00:34:53.030
No, that's yours, Nishizumi—

00:34:53.030 --> 00:34:55.660
You're the Commander now, Kawashima-senpai.

00:34:56.880 --> 00:34:58.290
Okay.

00:34:59.100 --> 00:35:01.780
Panzer vor!

00:35:44.400 --> 00:35:45.620
What the heck!?

00:35:45.620 --> 00:35:47.070
Did we run aground?

00:35:57.230 --> 00:35:59.020
The hell are you doing?!

00:35:59.020 --> 00:36:00.050
No way!

00:36:00.050 --> 00:36:05.490
They were just helping us get back to speed, Murakami. Right?

00:36:05.490 --> 00:36:08.370
Sorry, I rushed to conclusions. Thanks!

00:36:49.790 --> 00:36:51.160
Full stop!

00:36:59.230 --> 00:37:01.070
Very slow advance!

00:37:04.480 --> 00:37:08.680
This is Duck team! The enemy has found us! We are engaging!

00:37:13.550 --> 00:37:19.470
This is Leopon! They spotted us! We're buying time so the enemy won't go behind the main force!

00:38:00.190 --> 00:38:02.140
They're playing Pétanque...

00:38:02.140 --> 00:38:04.920
The flag tank's defense is also pretty lax...

00:38:04.920 --> 00:38:08.070
The enemy is absolutely open! We should go attack at once!

00:38:08.070 --> 00:38:09.350
Uh, sure!

00:38:22.390 --> 00:38:24.120
Slow advance!

00:38:54.550 --> 00:38:56.410
Slowly... Carefully...

00:38:57.690 --> 00:39:01.380
Keep the revs low so the enemy won't notice us.

00:39:05.840 --> 00:39:08.210
Has the bombardment started yet?

00:39:08.210 --> 00:39:12.760
They just said we're creeping towards them to cut off their head from behind.

00:39:12.760 --> 00:39:14.320
This feels underhanded.

00:39:14.320 --> 00:39:18.660
This is the plan Momo-san came up with. Let's pull it off flawlessly!

00:39:18.660 --> 00:39:20.830
They say that "with faith, even a sardine's head can be of value".

00:39:20.830 --> 00:39:23.420
Not that I have faith in sardines.

00:39:33.020 --> 00:39:34.910
What's wrong, Sodoko?

00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:40.190
Something feels off... like my Morals Committee sense is tingling...

00:39:44.810 --> 00:39:46.690
Contact at two-thirty!

00:39:46.690 --> 00:39:48.870
Hurry up and cross the bridge!

00:39:52.800 --> 00:39:54.290
Full reverse!

00:40:15.450 --> 00:40:19.930
Duck, Leopon! Rally up at point RK! We're surrounded!

00:40:19.930 --> 00:40:22.390
Damn it! This was a feint?!

00:40:22.940 --> 00:40:24.070
Leopon heading back!

00:40:24.070 --> 00:40:25.810
Can I use the EPS?

00:40:25.810 --> 00:40:28.880
Five seconds only. You'll burn the motor otherwise.

00:40:32.960 --> 00:40:35.350
This is like racing on an Indy oval track!

00:40:34.410 --> 00:40:36.810
I wish they reopen the oval tracks at Motegi...

00:40:36.810 --> 00:40:38.660
Is this really time for chit-chat?

00:40:38.660 --> 00:40:40.680
Protect the flag tank!

00:40:43.710 --> 00:40:47.770
What is this?! The enemy team is perfectly coordinated!

00:40:48.130 --> 00:40:49.250
This is bad!

00:40:49.440 --> 00:40:51.050
We've got nowehere to run!

00:40:52.420 --> 00:40:55.640
What's happening?! Wasn't BC supposed to be on bad terms with each other?!

00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:59.350
They were fighting in Yukari-san's recon video, weren't they?

00:40:59.350 --> 00:41:02.520
Maybe they knew we'd be doing recon in the first place!

00:41:02.680 --> 00:41:06.570
Then that means that their fighting was just an act to fool us!

00:41:06.570 --> 00:41:08.190
That may be the case.

00:41:08.540 --> 00:41:11.050
Played like a damn fiddle.

00:41:11.050 --> 00:41:13.070
That's because you underestimated us!

00:41:13.290 --> 00:41:19.390
I wonder which would happen first: Me finishing the cake, or their white flag popping up?

00:41:52.320 --> 00:41:55.380
Why?! Why?!

00:42:00.130 --> 00:42:03.920
I'm sorry, it's all my fault! I was completely fooled!

00:42:03.920 --> 00:42:06.360
This isn't your fault at all, Yukari-san!

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:09.370
But if this goes on, we'll drop out of the first match!

00:42:09.370 --> 00:42:11.090
That absolutely cannot happen!

00:42:11.090 --> 00:42:14.490
If that happens, it's the end of the road.

00:42:15.290 --> 00:42:18.390
Duck team ETA is five minutes, Leopon six!

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:19.920
They won't make it.

00:42:20.690 --> 00:42:23.470
Yukari-san, how long was the Mark IV again?

00:42:23.680 --> 00:42:26.930
8.04 meters! What about it?

00:42:28.560 --> 00:42:31.490
Shark team, I have a favor to ask!

00:42:31.490 --> 00:42:32.940
The Commander is Momo-san.

00:42:33.180 --> 00:42:36.930
Commander, please let the Shark team know...

00:42:36.930 --> 00:42:38.810
What is it?! Do you have a plan?!

00:42:38.810 --> 00:42:41.170
Operation "Hare of Inaba"!

00:42:45.530 --> 00:42:48.410
It's like walking the plank, 'eh?

00:42:48.410 --> 00:42:50.960
We be crossin' the rough seas! Are ye ready?!

00:42:50.960 --> 00:42:52.910
Steady she goes!

00:43:27.370 --> 00:43:29.620
Damn it! They're in my blind spot!

00:43:29.620 --> 00:43:32.150
Keep heading straight!

00:43:35.100 --> 00:43:37.400
They're getting away! Advance!

00:43:43.160 --> 00:43:45.170
Isn't this one too heavy?

00:43:53.450 --> 00:43:55.170
Okay! Let's go!

00:44:22.680 --> 00:44:24.100
Retreat!

00:44:35.940 --> 00:44:39.320
I'm sorry. I let my guard down.

00:44:39.320 --> 00:44:41.320
But I'm glad that everyone's safe.

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:43.360
Let's rework the plan.

00:44:44.080 --> 00:44:45.950
The second round's coming up!

00:44:45.950 --> 00:44:47.050
Okay!

